{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/udsvah03","slideIndex":0,"layout":{"id":"ly/ov6t8ra5","name":"BLANK"},"title":"Cloudflare 2019: what users experienced","textShapes":7,"backgroundColor":"rgba(19,32,52,1)"}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/x8r25obi","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":0,"top":0,"width":9.36,"height":540},"name":"Google Shape;235;p33","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/al0ja9sr","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":46.8,"top":34.56,"width":864.03,"height":44},"name":"Google Shape;236;p33","text":"Cloudflare 2019: what users experienced","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":30.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/vm9k3etc","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":50.4,"top":500.4,"width":648.03,"height":20},"name":"Google Shape;237;p33","text":"CASE 1","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":10.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/cre10zat","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":129.6,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;238;p33","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ds7i94by","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":120.24,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;239;p33","text":"Cloudflare sits between visitors and websites. Its servers deliver content and screen requests before they reach a website’s own server.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/58ja9kbi","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":203.04,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;240;p33","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/47qt0zax","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":193.68,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;241;p33","text":"On July 2, a firewall rule update overloaded servers worldwide. Visitors saw “502 Bad Gateway” errors instead of web pages.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/j6hs7utc","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":276.48,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;242;p33","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/i58bypsr","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":267.12,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;243;p33","text":"The outage lasted 27 minutes. CPU usage reached 100%, and Cloudflare’s traffic fell 82% at its worst.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/h4za5kb6","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":349.92,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;244;p33","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wjqtwfa1","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":340.56,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;245;p33","text":"Why it mattered: one shared provider’s failure interrupted many customers at once, even when their own websites were otherwise healthy.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/vihs3atg","slideIndex":0,"position":{"left":57,"top":457,"width":835,"height":27},"text":"Sources: Cloudflare incident update (July 2) and postmortem (July 12, 2019)","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11.51,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/udsvah03","slideIndex":0,"text":"Explain the setup as an intermediary: a visitor’s request passes through Cloudflare before reaching the site. A 502 error means that intermediary could not obtain the response it needed. The 82% figure describes Cloudflare’s traffic drop, not 82% of the Internet.\nAn everyday example: a visitor may be unable to open a store or complete an online task. This is an illustration of availability impact, not a measured financial-loss claim.\nSources: https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-outage/\nhttps://blog.cloudflare.com/details-of-the-cloudflare-outage-on-july-2-2019/"}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/m90b6t0r","slideIndex":1,"layout":{"id":"ly/ov6t8ra5","name":"BLANK"},"title":"The technical trigger: expensive pattern matching","textShapes":7,"backgroundColor":"rgba(19,32,52,1)"}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/ap43elwv","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":0,"top":0,"width":9.36,"height":540},"name":"Google Shape;250;p34","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/bqd47qd0","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":46.8,"top":34.56,"width":864.03,"height":44},"name":"Google Shape;251;p34","text":"The technical trigger: expensive pattern matching","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":30.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/crmlgvel","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":50.4,"top":500.4,"width":648.03,"height":20},"name":"Google Shape;252;p34","text":"CASE 1","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":10.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/xsfm90v6","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":129.6,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;253;p34","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/2143alwj","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":120.24,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;254;p34","text":"The web application firewall (WAF) checks requests for suspicious content. This update targeted malicious JavaScript.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/n2dk36d4","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":203.04,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;255;p34","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/o3mlcbep","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":193.68,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;256;p34","text":"A regular expression, or regex, is a text-search pattern. The simplified fragment .*.*=.* contains overlapping “match anything” sections.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/pov25gva","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":276.48,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;257;p34","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/exk361wn","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":267.12,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;258;p34","text":"Backtracking means retrying different ways to match the same text. Here, the repeated work consumed the CPU needed to serve requests.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/fytkz6d8","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":349.92,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;259;p34","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/j29072t0","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":340.56,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;260;p34","text":"“Simulate” mode only stopped the rule from blocking visitors. It still ran the expensive check on real traffic.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/i1gzexcf","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":57,"top":457,"width":835,"height":27},"text":"Sources: Cloudflare incident update and technical postmortem, July 2019","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11.51,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/m90b6t0r","slideIndex":1,"text":"Read the pattern aloud as: any text, followed by any text, followed by an equals sign, then any text. This is a simplified fragment, not the complete deployed expression.\nIllustrative example: when a candidate input lacks an equals sign, a backtracking matcher can repeatedly redistribute characters between the wildcard sections before deciding there is no match. A check can be logically correct yet too expensive to run on every request. Avoid calling this an infinite loop: the problem is excessive repeated work.\nSources: https://blog.cloudflare.com/details-of-the-cloudflare-outage-on-july-2-2019/\nhttps://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-outage/"}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/jetc3ut0","slideIndex":2,"layout":{"id":"ly/ov6t8ra5","name":"BLANK"},"title":"Why the safeguards did not catch it","textShapes":7,"backgroundColor":"rgba(19,32,52,1)"}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/6hsvqpwn","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":0,"top":0,"width":9.36,"height":540},"name":"Google Shape;265;p35","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/tkje1kfe","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":46.8,"top":34.56,"width":864.02,"height":44},"name":"Google Shape;266;p35","text":"Why the safeguards did not catch it","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":30.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8jadsfet","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":50.4,"top":500.4,"width":648.02,"height":20},"name":"Google Shape;267;p35","text":"CASE 1","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":10.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/re5wvexs","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":129.6,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;268;p35","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/qdwv29w7","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":120.24,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;269;p35","text":"Earlier refactoring accidentally removed a CPU safeguard. The effort to improve performance weakened a protection against costly rules.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/oj6twbup","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":203.04,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;270;p35","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/pkfapgva","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":193.68,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;271;p35","text":"Tests checked which requests to allow or block. They did not catch runaway CPU use, so passing tests gave incomplete reassurance.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/2xobu1cj","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":276.48,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;272;p35","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/nyxsn6d4","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":267.12,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;273;p35","text":"The rollout sent the rule worldwide without a limited trial. A local defect therefore became a global availability problem.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/cnqt0bul","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":349.92,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;274;p35","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/xozatgv6","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":340.56,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;275;p35","text":"Recovery also depended on affected systems. Engineers struggled to access internal tools, making an emergency change harder.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/alobylcf","slideIndex":2,"position":{"left":57,"top":457,"width":835,"height":27},"text":"Source: Cloudflare engineering postmortem, July 12, 2019","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11.51,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/jetc3ut0","slideIndex":2,"text":"Case analysis: several defenses failed together. A useful test plan asks both “Does this rule classify traffic correctly?” and “Can we afford to execute it under load?”\nA staged rollout exposes a small traffic sample first. Teams watch errors and CPU before expanding it. That limits how many customers encounter an undetected defect.\nThe debt connection is the accumulated risk in testing, deployment, and recovery procedures. The new regex triggered the incident, while existing weaknesses increased its severity.\nSource: https://blog.cloudflare.com/details-of-the-cloudflare-outage-on-july-2-2019/"}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/8f2psfyx","slideIndex":3,"layout":{"id":"ly/ov6t8ra5","name":"BLANK"},"title":"How engineers restored service","textShapes":7,"backgroundColor":"rgba(19,32,52,1)"}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/tgjed07a","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":0,"top":0,"width":9.36,"height":540},"name":"Google Shape;280;p36","geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/8vax4vqp","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":46.8,"top":34.56,"width":864.02,"height":44},"name":"Google Shape;281;p36","text":"How engineers restored service","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":30.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/7u1wbqp4","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":50.4,"top":500.4,"width":648.02,"height":20},"name":"Google Shape;282;p36","text":"CASE 1","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":10.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/lsze907y","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":129.6,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;284;p36","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/krqx0vqt","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":120.24,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;285;p36","text":"13:42 UTC: the rule goes live. By 14:00, engineers identify the WAF as the source of CPU exhaustion.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/jqhw7qp8","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":203.04,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;286;p36","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/yp8fyl8n","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":193.68,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;287;p36","text":"14:07 UTC: they disable the WAF globally. By 14:09, CPU usage and traffic return to normal.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/xoze5g72","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":276.48,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;288;p36","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wnqdwbqh","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":267.12,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;289;p36","text":"They roll back the faulty rule and test the fix. At 14:52 UTC, they restore the WAF worldwide.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/mt4b6hof","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":349.92,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;290;p36","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/nudcfm50","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":340.56,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;291;p36","text":"The tradeoff: websites recover before WAF inspection returns. Other security protections remain active during that interval.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ov6t8r6l","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":57,"top":457,"width":835,"height":27},"text":"Sources: Cloudflare incident update and engineering postmortem, July 2019","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11.51,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/8f2psfyx","slideIndex":3,"text":"All times refer to July 2, 2019, in UTC. A rollback restores an earlier configuration or version. Disabling the affected component first removes the immediate load, giving the team room to investigate.\nMake the two recovery milestones explicit: people could access websites again at 14:09, but the WAF returned at 14:52. Traffic recovery therefore does not mean every protection was already back. The detailed postmortem gives the 14:07 termination time and 14:00 diagnosis.\nSources: https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-outage/\nhttps://blog.cloudflare.com/details-of-the-cloudflare-outage-on-july-2-2019/"}
