{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/b250nutc","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":129.6,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;300;p37","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/a1wze9cr","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":120.24,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;301;p37","text":"Completed by July 12: restored the CPU safeguard and inspected all 3,868 managed rules for similar problems.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/x4nip4bi","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":203.04,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;302;p37","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/c3ehgzux","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":193.68,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;303;p37","text":"Planned testing: profile each rule’s performance. That means measuring its processing cost, beyond whether it gives the right answer.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/ny50jutg","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":276.48,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;304;p37","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/2dwzqpcv","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":267.12,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;305;p37","text":"Planned rollout: release rules in stages. Planned engine change: use RE2 or Rust regex with runtime guarantees.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/p0nil4bm","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":349.92,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;306;p37","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ozehczu1","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":340.56,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;307;p37","text":"Why the engine matters: RE2 bounds matching time linearly in input length for a fixed pattern, avoiding unbounded backtracking.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/fal0fat4","slideIndex":4,"position":{"left":57,"top":457,"width":835,"height":27},"text":"Sources: Cloudflare postmortem (July 12, 2019) and Google RE2 documentation","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11.51,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/hgzapcr6","slideIndex":4,"text":"The first bullet describes work reported complete. The following actions were announced in the July 12 postmortem, so this slide does not claim they had all shipped by that date.\nRE2 explanation: for a fixed pattern, work scales proportionally with input length instead of exploding through repeated retries. This does not mean every expression takes the same time. RE2 also restricts syntax: features such as backreferences and look-around are unsupported. A migration therefore needs compatibility tests.\nSources: https://blog.cloudflare.com/details-of-the-cloudflare-outage-on-july-2-2019/\nhttps://github.com/google/re2"}
