{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/j2xcnut0","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":50.4,"top":500.4,"width":648.02,"height":20},"name":"Google Shape;314;p38","text":"CASE 1","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":10.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/54zep4bq","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":129.6,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;316;p38","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/k3qdgzul","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":120.24,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;317;p38","text":"Maintenance includes keeping changes safe. Fixing the broken rule restores service, while stronger tests help prevent another failure.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/3y1wzyt4","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":203.04,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;318;p38","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/2dsvqtcj","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":193.68,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;319;p38","text":"Technical debt can live in processes too. Saving time on rollout or testing can create larger debugging and outage costs later.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/ytwzyxwr","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":276.48,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;320;p38","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/zu5gridc","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":267.12,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;321;p38","text":"Refactoring should preserve behavior. Teams also need regression tests for safety limits that ordinary feature tests may miss.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/0vehknex","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":64.8,"top":349.92,"width":7.92,"height":7.92},"name":"Google Shape;322;p38","geometry":"roundRect","fillColor":"#189D94","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":18.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#000000","alignment":"center"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/lwnytsvi","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":88.56,"top":340.56,"width":792.02,"height":61.6},"name":"Google Shape;323;p38","text":"Practical takeaway: test correctness and resource use, expand releases gradually, and rehearse recovery when normal tools are unavailable.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22.67,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F7F9FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/mxwzmxw3","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":57,"top":457,"width":835,"height":27},"text":"Case analysis, informed by Cloudflare’s postmortem and Martin Fowler on refactoring","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":11.51,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#9DACBC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/6lsnupw7","slideIndex":5,"text":"These are the presentation’s conclusions from the case. Corrective maintenance addresses an existing defect. Preventive maintenance reduces the likelihood of future failures.\nRefactoring changes a program’s internal structure while preserving external behavior. The case shows why a team must identify the protections that need to survive a code change. A proposed regression test could run difficult inputs and fail when a rule exceeds an agreed processing budget. This is a recommendation, not a claim about Cloudflare’s exact implementation.\nDiscussion question: If a change returns the same answers but makes the service unavailable under load, has it preserved the behavior users need?\nConcept source: https://refactoring.com/\nCase evidence: https://blog.cloudflare.com/details-of-the-cloudflare-outage-on-july-2-2019/"}